This repo builds `vis42.mcpb`, a one-click MCP Bundle for Claude Desktop. It contains a Node.js stdio-to-HTTP proxy that forwards all MCP operations to `https://vis42.com/api/mcp` (see MCPB MANIFEST.md + README).

Proxy behavior:
- Must answer Claude Desktop `initialize` immediately.
- Remote connection is deferred/lazy; do not connect during startup.

Use lazy remote connect:
```js
async function getRemoteClient() {
if (remoteClient) return remoteClient;
if (connectPromise) return connectPromise;
connectPromise = (async () => { /* connect, set remoteClient */ })();
}
server.setRequestHandler(ListToolsRequestSchema, async (req) => {
const client = await getRemoteClient(); // lazy
return await client.listTools(req.params);
});
```

Transport constructors never throw. Errors surface only when `client.connect()` is awaited. SSE fallback must wrap the `connect()` call:
```js
const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(url, { requestInit: { headers } });
await client.connect(transport);
log(`StreamableHTTP failed (${err.message}), retrying with SSE...`);
const sseTransport = new SSEClientTransport(url, { requestInit: { headers } });
